{
  "slug": "palliative-and-advance-care-planning-in-pd",
  "concept": "Palliative and advance care planning in PD",
  "generated": "2026-11-27",
  "summary": "Source-anchored research for Palliative and advance care planning in PD. Run status: COMPLETED.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Structure and components",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Advance care planning includes clarifying values, choosing a surrogate, discussing future medical care and documenting preferences; paperwork is one part of the process. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6556088/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:14888003d6ba9088263eb72a0e6cb49f161b597173adb40d41bdb4ac08b4e09f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4bdb71b14ce94fe1b76c990ca768371414377c9310b86c21ff3b6ff60736e3dc",
            "ev:b994ac6062f5f91094c80e5f1cad51483f1e578e56c4e10271cd5d5b0ddabf78"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng71/chapter/recommendations"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Advance care planning is a continuing discussion of future care needs, wishes and preferences, including decisions for a time when a person may be unable to decide independently. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8355553/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:55ffddb4b92d8604a271559d4547d350875e9a850f53ace72d522844008685fc",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:396c6be13fae26b77c7c95cfc74300c89da9f8ba3dc89dc968b4cc5aa150a928",
            "ev:5cbc224d8e6b2258add3d6b34ea12012a74c3d160c7d77e53a6ab6b3a6a2c87e"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13771020/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Individual readiness and timing matter: interview findings support regularly revisiting information preferences, while the PD_Pal contextual analysis found both resistance when discussion felt premature and cognitive limitations that could obstruct later participation. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8355553/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:80cf3aaee43dd69021d25ba1ec64c1cdd6eb5f71c27dbe3c326f23242a57cae8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b113248370477a20e0321fe0e920d5c5a393ae7f2cf7915e2ce048320a2d8510",
            "ev:fe88a2a49e3bd742c4b628e9e965fb5a720c87a824738eadadc4b39e86427af0"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13771020/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "PD_Pal’s authors identify fragmented electronic-record documentation and limited visibility as possible reasons recorded preferences may be missed; documentation alone may not capture the quality or process of ACP discussions. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13771020/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:bb2a06226c35031e57ba62eac020d28a0aba46bfae6e7d31d5127ace57d4bf3c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:ef859f578220144f908af51f65bf8cb223679203ba5b95b555caefae34c65a84"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The 2020 randomized trial enrolled 210 people with PD or related disorders with moderate-to-high palliative needs; at 6 months the palliative-care group had better quality of life (treatment effect 1.87; 95% CI 0.47–3.27). Its mixed diagnostic population and selected needs limit extrapolation to all PD patients. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7042842/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0e05798aae2a3ba1f06ddf59784e21497cee5f0d25087245041745175c93ba8f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3f316bf8e3e302a55b3889f00138d863cae2951f92ca264ef75a53142d67fcae",
            "ev:50a05f29e8df94cc9a1561be2f7035c061280f3c9b94ba88440a95990cc3e349",
            "ev:de936b172c328c4f3b840d34cf6fb632dee6b4f48217322331340e18e487f289"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The 2020 trial found improved advance-directive completion among secondary outcomes, but its lack of demographic diversity and conduct at experienced academic centers limit generalizability. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7042842/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5087420bf8b41d50877ce818426e88ed4a43add5b0fd7cd4c6573c2932151ba2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6f0c8d8185aa13d06f0f192587ec7334ae64cce21375eb8c87619994f1252db8",
            "ev:de936b172c328c4f3b840d34cf6fb632dee6b4f48217322331340e18e487f289"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Lum and colleagues recommend starting ACP discussions early because later communication and cognitive difficulties can reduce participation; they also recommend checking readiness, knowledge and information needs rather than assuming everyone wants the same discussion. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6556088/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c244fafdede811b08a479e89423855f683e5447fa4077a6824279e9a0b275f93",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1a6f13269f96c254b42c038e9173ff97e76c2317e60c12e3d08e93260df9c978",
            "ev:1ec38ac053f849763617e02d9dc662ca055a41479f239b4970becde2424b1c07",
            "ev:554d413fcf924b8104fe3f2c68c36f0591b007089feba55736d5a13a37fcc341",
            "ev:bfa45c4f12fdd3e829bab19b6465607f10299538884fa784a63589a947501cda"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In that 2020 trial, among participants without an advance directive at baseline, six-month completion was 53% with palliative care versus 26% with standard care; the health-care-proxy completion comparison was not significant. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7042842/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3e0f1dcd995a3ea04286181819fb20d1f0df42d2b8ca53a60c508cf6cc5ac250",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3914494747e6f8fe49762a97567715020610bcdd8f992a5fa7f4284cf1cc95d9",
            "ev:de936b172c328c4f3b840d34cf6fb632dee6b4f48217322331340e18e487f289"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the 2021 qualitative interview study of 20 patients, most wanted ACP discussion with a clinician and the majority preferred clinician initiation early in the disease; preferred information timing varied. These are participant perspectives rather than evidence that everyone wants immediate detailed end-of-life planning. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8355553/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0aa603e9cbd2ee1a9027c540a9c0fba31e7e5b3fe65a933cb4b80ac348f0013d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:06dcb9b6338b5abbc40076d1c063857a58633bc2b96bae8ccde8df64649f09a0",
            "ev:16edbd0eda25f32d82d3668855d47db89a8f29c8d077b7c2dcfe645b4dd80538"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Palliative care addresses symptoms, psychosocial concerns and future planning; NICE recommends considering referral at any stage of PD, so it need not wait until the terminal phase. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7042842/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:8a6e81841be489a2cdaaa31a833d9e98b223a93497458c8aa65898c18c9ef0e5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2a16e45b5a675631249779fdb22e8211a5c25180628b893cbad6a8fff00dc65d",
            "ev:a2e5314f8035974a72cf9c2ce230e43cea04d48ae4fe9b8eba480fb39b92cc9e"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng71/chapter/recommendations"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NICE’s 2017 PD recommendations advise oral and written information about progression, future treatment options and end-of-life issues, with the discussion recorded; named UK planning mechanisms include ADRT, DNACPR and Lasting Power of Attorney. These are UK guideline examples, not universal legal instruments. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng71/chapter/recommendations",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e32a9f00632fdc1a2bedf9075e22d34d7bce63f4f88988a0def5792bcf0f87ba",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:530a4e40b0e0f6c6adcb9b03116d62765456354b715f9e319da28d1dcc6ba057"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the 2026 PD_Pal trial, 189 participants with advanced parkinsonism were randomized to a six-month nurse-led ACP and care-coordination intervention or usual care; documented end-of-life preferences did not differ significantly at six months (P=0.77). This trial does not establish that structured ACP universally improves documentation. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13771020/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f3b9df6b0ceff0f061456c6f21ecd74e88776da8f4cd0a8cdca807e204cf3759",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:98618c5ac8a09b67448b51343478811287df6f060344150e35d2a7172f89e474",
            "ev:dc60afdb0ba379296c4a2e5f721a7a612a46edfeaf232ec3967ade4b56e5f1ff"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Benefits in one palliative-care trial should not be generalized to every ACP intervention: the 2020 intervention improved advance-directive completion, whereas PD_Pal in 2026 did not improve its primary documentation endpoint. They tested different interventions and populations. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7042842/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:04b5583cf2175f7a64a4ab6f00898349c7dc0839e8c08b39b3ad34adac1e9b92",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6c97409af0cd845db07d6c8f05609e299e25d8566551f23857116c379e0d4127",
            "ev:98618c5ac8a09b67448b51343478811287df6f060344150e35d2a7172f89e474",
            "ev:ca11014ef6d978e1968f9d823b1c1d071e9c72af572bcccfebb89f1856068532",
            "ev:de936b172c328c4f3b840d34cf6fb632dee6b4f48217322331340e18e487f289"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13771020/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The 2020 trial did not demonstrate a significant between-group reduction in healthcare use; the authors cautioned that relevant events were few. Reduced hospitalization should not be presented as an established result of that trial. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7042842/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:201d60d8c1c9b057920676863f73ae371a5a648b1f6c1c9791cba31846af2824",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5414adb6ac0cac3923d188789845f3881342c1a35dfbd5cb3383ccf8354b1088",
            "ev:de936b172c328c4f3b840d34cf6fb632dee6b4f48217322331340e18e487f289"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Generalizability of the 2020 trial is limited by experienced academic sites, a population lacking diversity and an unblinded design with possible patient-reported-outcome bias. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7042842/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0ddb1380b986626bc1ffaa958606f4981f406ead29329ea66751118bb68c47c9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9df70827e4f4ccc16e0614feed1e6a2f5ad1cec16e016f52f9fc52e2a0fc5cea",
            "ev:de936b172c328c4f3b840d34cf6fb632dee6b4f48217322331340e18e487f289"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NICE recommends prognosis discussions that promote patient priorities and shared decisions, and recognition that relatives may have different information needs from the person with PD. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng71/chapter/recommendations",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f8f29cb27a1115801692f92a125fa8605f1570c74ff93d7dc63694a0f37b8054",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:14fda23550d0b5fc5a1652869e4af4ceb5c64edc1988b17e8cff96e1d635554d",
            "ev:6f16419065e4d5074ca50a066e44c6502e790514554e071441bea42bbd96d5e5"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
