      "documentConcept": "Palliative and advance care planning in PD",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:750582b8428f258f0db36e86c2956c94b9b3400186b82262be7341fef750c420",
      "text": "Palliative care in PD supports quality of life, symptom relief and planning throughout illness. ACP addresses values, future treatment preferences, surrogate decision-making and documentation. NICE recommends opportunities for prognosis discussions and considering palliative referral at any stage. Trial results depend on the intervention: a 2020 outpatient palliative-care trial improved quality of life and advance-directive completion, while the 2026 PD_Pal trial did not improve its primary documentation endpoint. Early, repeated conversations should account for readiness and possible future cognitive or communication difficulties. The claims below distinguish guideline recommendations, qualitative findings and trial-specific outcomes.",
